This has been suggested before, but to tell whether this is a myth or
a fact would require more in-depth understanding of the monster
generation code than I have.  After looking at
http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/mon2-343.txt I can see how it
might apply to random monster generation - Moloch's Sanctum can never
appear above D:45, so if you are at least level 14, all monsters of
difficulty level 29 or below (that is, all monsters which can occur
randomly at all) are eligible for generation.

Even so, I'd wonder about other sorts of monster generation.  Does
your XL make any difference at all to the "summon nasties" effect?
What about random monsters of a fixed class - the Astral Plane
contains "three random L" and if you were playing genocideless you
might want to slant the probabilities towards the weaker varieties of
lich.
